######## 59. One plain-string secret under an AWS prefix (api, environment qa)

$ kagebunshin project add-env api qa
added environment qa to project api

$ kagebunshin project add-source api qa --provider aws_sm --prefix acme/dev/ --profile acme-dev
added a source to environment qa of project api; it replaces the default source, the local store's section, unless you add `--provider file` too

$ kagebunshin --env qa status
daemon: unlocked
providers:
  aws_sm  profile acme-dev  ok
project: api
env: qa
4 keys
  API_KEY       aws_sm:acme/dev/api
  API_URL       aws_sm:acme/dev/api
  DATABASE_URL  aws_sm:acme/dev/db
  QUEUE_URL     aws_sm:acme/dev/queue  not in .env.example
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  SIGNING_KEY
  LOG_LEVEL
to fill in what is missing:
  you can run:
    kagebunshin project add-source api qa --provider aws_sm --secret acme/dev/signing --key NAME --profile acme-dev
      (secret acme/dev/signing is not a JSON object, so it was skipped; this adds its whole string as one key, if NAME is replaced with the key's name)
    kagebunshin project set-var api qa LOG_LEVEL info
      (only if .env.example's value is the real setting, not a placeholder; a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
warning: aws_sm prefix acme/dev/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret acme/dev/signing, which is not a JSON object

$ kagebunshin --env qa diff
project: api
env: qa
missing (in .env.example, set by no source):
  SIGNING_KEY
  LOG_LEVEL
extra (set by a source, not in .env.example): 1 key
  aws_sm:acme/dev/queue  1 key
to fill in what is missing:
  you can run:
    kagebunshin project add-source api qa --provider aws_sm --secret acme/dev/signing --key NAME --profile acme-dev
      (secret acme/dev/signing is not a JSON object, so it was skipped; this adds its whole string as one key, if NAME is replaced with the key's name)
    kagebunshin project set-var api qa LOG_LEVEL info
      (only if .env.example's value is the real setting, not a placeholder; a secret belongs in the store or a provider)
warning: aws_sm prefix acme/dev/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret acme/dev/signing, which is not a JSON object
kagebunshin: 2 keys in .env.example are not set by any source
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin --env qa run -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: warning: aws_sm prefix acme/dev/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret acme/dev/signing, which is not a JSON object
kagebunshin: warning: 2 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: SIGNING_KEY, LOG_LEVEL
ok   API_KEY
ok   API_URL
ok   DATABASE_URL
MISSING SIGNING_KEY
MISSING LOG_LEVEL
[exit 1]

$ kagebunshin --env qa run --strict -- ./test.sh
kagebunshin: warning: aws_sm prefix acme/dev/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret acme/dev/signing, which is not a JSON object
kagebunshin: 2 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: SIGNING_KEY, LOG_LEVEL
[exit 1]

-- 58: with --json, the warning is JSON too

$ kagebunshin --json --env qa run -- true
{"warning":"aws_sm prefix acme/dev/ (profile acme-dev): skipped secret acme/dev/signing, which is not a JSON object"}
{"warning":"2 keys in .env.example are not set by any source: SIGNING_KEY, LOG_LEVEL"}

-- the fix the warning names, with no sync after it

$ kagebunshin project add-source api qa --provider aws_sm --secret acme/dev/signing --key SIGNING_KEY --profile acme-dev
added a source to environment qa of project api

$ kagebunshin project set-var api qa LOG_LEVEL info
set LOG_LEVEL for environment qa of project api

$ kagebunshin --env qa run --strict -- ./test.sh
ok   API_KEY
ok   API_URL
ok   DATABASE_URL
ok   SIGNING_KEY
ok   LOG_LEVEL

$ kagebunshin --env qa next
project api, environment qa: done. 5 of 5 keys set; `./test.sh` ran with them on <day>. They come from aws_sm:acme/dev/api (2), aws_sm:acme/dev/db (1), aws_sm:acme/dev/signing (1), the project file (1).
